and impact on patients and the healthcare system", "abstract": "Malnutrition is a debilitating and highly prevalent 
condition in the acute hospital setting, with Australian and international studies reporting rates of approximately 40%.
Malnutrition is associated with many adverse outcomes including depression of the immune system, impaired wound healing,
